// Lexical scoping, loop shape: the flat loop test.
//
// The site is bounded (nothing leaves the activation) and plain, but its byte
// count is a variable, so no pool can own a fixed slot and the stack cannot
// measure it. Psi-2 would have prepared one arena for the whole frame and held
// every iteration's block until the function returned. Here the arena is created
// on the edge into the loop and destroyed on the edge out of it, so the loop's
// storage dies with the loop.
//
// The `if` before the loop is deliberate: it makes the loop's preheader a block
// of its own, so the create cannot be mistaken for entry-block prologue code.
int function main() {
    var total = 0;
    var index = 0;
    var count = 8192;
    if (total == 0) {
        print(0);
    }
    while (index < 4) {
        var value = memory.allocate<int>(count);
        value[0] = index;
        total = total + value[0];
        index = index + 1;
    }
    print(total);
    return 0;
}
